Kampung contains no third-party source code. Its starting idea comes from
claude-peers-mcp (https://github.com/louislva/claude-peers-mcp, MIT License),
which lets Claude Code sessions on one machine find and message each other
through an MCP server. Kampung was written from scratch to do the same across
machines, with its own server, keys, pairing and audit log.
